MAYOR OF PALANGKA RAYA,

Considering a. that every citizen has the right to survival, growth, and proper development and to obtain consistent and systematic security as a form of Protection for Women and Children as mandated in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

b. that Regional Government, families, groups, social organizations and/or other community organizations have responsibility for the implementation of fulfillment, protection, respect, advancement and enforcement of rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

c. that to provide direction, legal foundation and legal certainty in the Protection of Women and Children, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence;

Bearing in mind 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 of 1965 concerning the Establishment of the Municipality of Palangka Raya (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1965 Number 48, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2753);

